  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nTomorrow night will be the coolest night of the week with a few \nareas along the Plateau may dropping into the 50s.\n\nFriday will be another beautiful day with slightly warmer\ntemperatures but comfortable humidity. The pattern will become \nmore unsettled Friday night and into Saturday morning as an upper \nlevel low digs southwest out of the Northern Plains and into the\nTN/OH Valleys. Medium to high chances for showers and storms will\nlinger through the weekend with QPF currently ranging from\n0.5-1.5\" across the area. There's still not much of a signal for\nsevere weather, but this will be monitored over the coming days.\n\nLow to medium chances for showers and storms will continue through\nmid-week with temperatures becoming increasingly warm. By \nWednesday, we'll be back in the mid-80s to low-90s. With higher \nhumidity as well, heat indices in the upper-90s to low-100s will \nbe possible.",
